69,2,1,talk,Minako,,"Kenji has been executed, and Mizuki was attacked. This is a critical development. The fact that Mizuki was targeted suggests the werewolf viewed her as a threat or wanted to remove a strong logical voice. What are your thoughts on this?","{""words"":41,""mentions"":[""Kenji"",""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,2,1,talk,Shizue,,"Oh, what a terrible tragedy. Poor Mizuki-san... she was so passionate about protecting us. It is truly heartbreaking to lose two of our friends so quickly. I hope we can find the strength to move forward together.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"It is indeed a tragedy, though a revealing one. The werewolf's decision to eliminate Mizuki-san immediately after Kenji-san's execution suggests a desire to remove those who were most vocal in the conflict. It effectively silences the logic she championed.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Mizuki"",""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,2,2,talk,Minako,,"@Benjamin, I agree. The werewolf has effectively cleared the board of the most contentious voices. With Kenji and Mizuki gone, we are left with Shizue and yourself. @Shizue, you've been very quiet. Do you have any observations?","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Benjamin"",""Kenji"",""Mizuki"",""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,2,2,talk,Shizue,,"I have simply been praying for our safety, Minako-san. It is so frightening to think the wolf is still among us. I only hope that we can trust one another now, so we may end this sadness.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"While trust is a comforting thought, Shizue-san, we must remain vigilant. The werewolf's strategy has been remarkably efficient. By removing the most disruptive elements, they have created a facade of peace. We must ask: who benefits most from this sudden tranquility?","{""words"":41,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,2,3,talk,Minako,,"@Benjamin, you've hit on the core issue. The current peace is artificial. @Shizue, your desire for trust is kind, but in this game, it can be a shield for the werewolf. If you aren't the wolf, what evidence can you provide?","{""words"":41,""mentions"":[""Benjamin"",""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,2,3,talk,Shizue,,"Oh, Minako-san, it pains me that my kindness is seen as a shield. I have no evidence other than my heart's desire for peace. I am just a simple woman who wishes for this nightmare to end.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"A heart's desire is a poetic sentiment, Shizue-san, but alas, it is not a verifiable fact. In a game of deception, the absence of evidence is not evidence of innocence, but rather a void that a wolf might comfortably inhabit.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,2,4,talk,Minako,,"@Benjamin, your analysis is precise. @Shizue, while I appreciate your nature, your lack of a logical defense is now a liability. Between the two of you, Benjamin has consistently provided analysis. Shizue, your silence is too convenient. I suspect you.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[""Benjamin"",""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,2,4,talk,Shizue,,"Oh, Minako-san, it brings tears to my eyes that you would think so of me. I only wish to be a source of comfort in these dark times. Please, let us not let suspicion tear us apart.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
80,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,"It is a poignant scene, certainly. However, we must remember that the werewolf's most effective disguise is often the one that evokes the most sympathy. Logic dictates that we cannot let emotion cloud our final judgment.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
